<title>USA: UPS says no progress in talks.</title>
<headline>UPS says no progress in talks.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service of America Inc. said Wednesday there has been no progress in negotiations with the International Brotherhood of Teamsters.</p>
<p>&quot;No significant developments have arisen,&quot; the company said in a statement on the company's Web site.</p>
<p>UPS said it would continue &quot;on a daily basis&quot; to negotiate a new labor agreement with the Teamsters. The current contract expires Thursday.</p>
<p>A spokesman said Tuesday that the company's package volume has declined during the past two months. The company said it cannot promise it will be able to continue to complete deliveries after Thursday.</p>
</text>
